Subject: [PATCH 1/5] docs: add lower-window execution plan for coupling
 pre-validation

Self-contained plan for the execution window covering the gates that must
close before any coupling interface is frozen or trained:

- T0 push the local backlog and reconcile the withdrawn compute figures
- T1 (P0) build the multi-horizon persistent-failure set; the h20/h50
  records already in logs/upper_na_f1/ give an intersection of
  {262005, 262006}, both ending on the 50 deg field-of-view limit
- T2-T4 (P1) scan hold radius, approach rate and lateral offset through the
  existing scripted-upper-layer harness, reporting the full grid rather than
  a rescued/not-rescued verdict, plus fuel per cell
- T5 (P2) check whether the existing MPC step diagnostics separate rescued
  from unrescued commands, before spending training seeds on an ablation

Records the stop conditions, the serial-compute and single-factor rules, and
which stages need user authorisation.

