Subject: [PATCH 2/5] docs: lower-window execution plan for pre-design
 validation (rev.2)

Self-contained plan for the lower execution window covering T0-T5
pre-design validation, with T6/T7 held behind an explicit gate.

Incorporates five review corrections:
- T2 split into a commit-time control layer and a hold-radius increment
  layer so the rescue is attributable to one variable at a time.
- T5 feedback quantities audited: solver status, slack and actuator usage
  are free; predicted_minimum_margin requires runtime_diagnostics and a
  full horizon rollout, so it is offline-diagnostic only until audited.
- T5 separability is a three-layer check (distribution, time evolution,
  early warning), not a single-layer veto.
- T7 no longer pre-labels the long-horizon row as over budget; that is
  decided by the T1 deployment-equivalent re-measurement.
- T0 written conditionally: the local/remote divergence is to be verified
  locally, not asserted as an upper-level checked fact.

