From 0b9ec5d59c7df13c38e2122ad07a8263c84642be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 16:02:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat: freeze the T6 arrival-condition coupling interface

A 2D upper-layer action naming an arrival condition, resolved to the
unchanged 3D waypoint channel, plus a 3D execution-feedback channel that
closes the loop back from the optimiser to the policy. No controller,
dynamics, task or reward change.

Action channels follow what T2-T4 actually measured: commit timing was the
only variable that rescued a persistently failing seed, the hold radius was
the only one that moved fuel, lateral adjustment rescued nothing and gets no
channel. The blend interpolates direction and radius separately rather than
chording between two points, because the offline feasibility plan that
solves the hardest seed stages on the approach axis and a chord at the same
radius is still dominated by the far hold end.

The commit end is the fixed-setpoint controller, and this is proven rather
than asserted: over twelve seeds and 300 control steps each, the wrench from
a = (+1, .) through the wrapper matches a directly constructed fixed
reference with max |delta| = 0.

Feedback carries only quantities that fall out of the solve: fallback
fraction, peak slack read exclusively from steps that solved, and mean
actuator usage. The predicted-margin diagnostic is excluded because it needs
a horizon rollout the deployment path does not pay for, and because it is a
prediction rather than a truth margin.

Also records the 262006 finding: the offline certificate completes it in
217.5 s with zero truth violations and 0.693 rad of field-of-view margin, so
it is not at a reachability boundary, but 42 further interface cells fail
exactly as the earlier position scans did. That failure is a pointing
failure, and a position-only upper channel cannot address it. Left as a
separate candidate factor, not folded in here.

Full regression 211 passed.

